# The Elastic global navigation script loads and renders its header on a published docs site.
# Ported from the second step of synthetics/journeys/navigation-test.journey.ts. The old step also checked the
# min-height that #elastic-nav-wrapper reserves at three widths, which journeys cannot assert yet (`get styles` only
# reads), so that part stays in TypeScript.
# @tags chrome
# @requires build-type:assembler
open ./
wait --load networkidle
expect visible "#elastic-nav-wrapper"
expect request "**/elastic-nav.js" --status 2xx
expect visible find role navigation --name Main
